== unit-of-work {"renames":0,"otherTabSaves":1}: 5 frames
  [0] Flank left and Hold the ridge are read from the store. Both are clean: they sit in no register, and the unit notes the version each was read at.
  [1] The operator creates Night march. The unit registers it as new; nothing is written yet.
  [2] The operator deletes Flank left. It moves to the removed register; its row stays in the store until the commit.
  [3] Another tab saves its own rename of Hold the ridge. The store now has version 6, while this session still holds version 5.
  [4] The save commits once: a single call carries insert Night march, delete Flank left, and every register is empty again.
