== pessimistic-offline-lock {"tabASaves":0,"timeout":5}: 5 frames
  [0] Tab A asks for the lock on Hold the ridge, gets it and reads version 4. The lock is its own until minute 5.
  [1] Tab B asks for the lock, but Tab A holds it, so it is turned away at once, before it has changed anything, and told who has it.
  [2] Tab A's lock ran out at minute 5, so Tab B, after waiting 3 minutes, takes it over and reads version 4. Tab A no longer holds the composition.
  [3] Tab A is closed. Its lock had already been taken over, so there is nothing to release.
  [4] Tab B still owns the lock, so it writes version 5 and releases the lock.
== pessimistic-offline-lock {"tabASaves":0,"timeout":20}: 5 frames
  [0] Tab A asks for the lock on Hold the ridge, gets it and reads version 4. The lock is its own until minute 20.
  [1] Tab B asks for the lock, but Tab A holds it, so it is turned away at once, before it has changed anything, and told who has it.
  [2] Tab A is closed without saving or releasing. Its lock stays taken until minute 20, keeping the other tab out.
  [3] Tab A's lock ran out at minute 20, so Tab B, after waiting 18 minutes, takes it over and reads version 4. Tab A no longer holds the composition.
  [4] Tab B still owns the lock, so it writes version 5 and releases the lock.
